    "source_notes": "CORRECTION: Punaluʻu Beach Park IS lifeguarded — it appears on the official State of Hawaiʻi Ocean Safety 'List of Lifeguarded Beaches' (oceansafety.hawaii.gov) under Hawaiʻi Island, hours listed Mon-Sun 9:30am-4:45pm; visitor guides report 8:30am-5pm. The draft's claim that no Kaʻū beach is guarded was WRONG. Set lg:'seasonal'/staffed but kept warning_only because of a documented 2014 drowning, boat-channel rip, freshwater-spring shock, and high-surf exposure (Hawaii247/county news, lovebigisland, NWS). Facing ~SE (150°) matches the SE Kaʻū coastline. Coordinates 19.1360/-155.5040 confirmed (latitude.to/Wikipedia). VERIFY exact current lifeguard hours/days locally. NEEDS-HUMAN-VERIFY",
